Subject: [PATCH] platform/chrome: cros_ec_typec: mark AP-driven altmodes for mode selection

The DisplayPort alternate-mode driver may request mode entry as soon as a
partner mode binds.  On systems where the EC requires AP-driven mode entry,
that races the userspace policy owner and can select DisplayPort before USB4
capability discovery is coherent.

Use the connector class mode-selection flag for partner and plug modes when
the EC advertises AP-driven entry.  Drivers still bind and explicit sysfs
activation remains available; automatic mode entry is suppressed only for
systems that requested AP ownership.

This changes no device matching and introduces no private EC protocol.

---
 drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_typec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_typec.c b/drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_typec.c
index 000000000000..111111111111 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_typec.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_typec.c
@@ -725,6 +725,7 @@ static int cros_typec_register_altmodes(struct cros_typec_data *typec, int port_
 			desc.svid = sop_disc->svids[i].svid;
 			desc.mode = j + 1;
 			desc.vdo = sop_disc->svids[i].mode_vdo[j];
+			desc.mode_selection = typec->ap_driven_altmode;
 
 			if (is_partner)
 				amode = typec_partner_register_altmode(port->partner, &desc);
-- 
2.51.0
